{"parentUuid":"16b679a5-6df1-489d-b027-ee2924133529","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"8caa67d2-997c-4b7f-ab12-8ec84fe807a8","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"snug-orbiting-fountain","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_vrtx_01CsN3badvWyCaR7NPXGaBEb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Msq81ysNj3ediWULByJjEd","name":"Task","input":{"subagent_type":"general-purpose","description":"Extract schema from format.pdf","prompt":"Read the /app/workspace/data/format.pdf file and extract the schema information for:\n1. Task events - what are the column names and their meanings (especially timestamp, job ID, task index, event type)\n2. Job events - what are the column names and their meanings (especially timestamp, job ID, event type)\n\nFocus on understanding which columns contain the timestamp (in microseconds), job ID, task index, and event type fields. Also identify what event type value represents a SUBMIT event."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1590,"cache_read_input_tokens":33594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1590,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXb4h9nnmhSncrdPKMPhH","type":"assistant","uuid":"c92a5d0c-a318-470b-966f-27d2be116b70","timestamp":"2026-01-29T04:48:28.166Z"}
{"parentUuid":"c92a5d0c-a318-470b-966f-27d2be116b70","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"8caa67d2-997c-4b7f-ab12-8ec84fe807a8","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"snug-orbiting-fountain","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01Msq81ysNj3ediWULByJjEd","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have all the information needed. Let me create a comprehensive summary document.\n\n## Schema Information Extraction Summary\n\nBased on my analysis of the Google Cluster Trace 2011-2 dataset at `/app/workspace/data/`, I've successfully extracted the schema information for both Task Events and Job Events tables.\n\n---\n\n## 1. TASK EVENTS TABLE SCHEMA\n\n**File Location:** `/app/workspace/data/task_events/part-00001-of-00500.csv.gz`\n\n**Total Columns:** 13\n\n### Column Definitions:\n\n| Column | Name | Data Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-----------|-------------|\n| 1 | **timestamp** | Integer (64-bit) | Event timestamp in **microseconds** since 600 seconds before trace start (May 1, 2011 19:00 EDT) |\n| 2 | missing_info | String | Empty string when no missing data; otherwise contains missing data indicators |\n| 3 | **job_id** | Integer | Unique identifier for the job |\n| 4 | **task_index** | Integer | 0-based index of the task within the job |\n| 5 | machine_id | Integer | ID of the machine where the task is/was running (empty for SUBMIT events) |\n| 6 | **event_type** | Integer | Type of event (see event types below) |\n| 7 | user | String (Base64) | Hashed username for confidentiality |\n| 8 | scheduling_class | Integer | Latency sensitivity: 0=free, 1=best effort, 2-3=mid-tier, 4+=production |\n| 9 | priority | Integer | Priority level (0-11, where higher = more important) |\n| 10 | cpu_request | Float | Requested CPU cores (normalized) |\n| 11 | memory_request | Float | Requested memory (normalized) |\n| 12 | disk_space_request | Float | Requested disk space (normalized) |\n| 13 | different_machines_restriction | Boolean | 0 or 1 indicating if tasks must run on different machines |\n\n### Event Type Values for Task Events:\n- **0 = SUBMIT** - Task is submitted to the system\n- **1 = SCHEDULE** - Task is scheduled on a machine\n- **2 = EVICT** - Task is evicted from a machine\n- **3 = FAIL** - Task fails\n- **4 = KILL** - Task is killed\n- **5 = FINISH** - Task completes successfully\n\n**Sample Task Event (SUBMIT):**\n```\n5612587446,,6251995937,33,,0,4Ubmtvv/epOnUEgegvGV9mCxxcZkV4z/Dm8RY/9SEYw=,0,0,0.06873,0.01193,0.0001154,0\n```\n- Timestamp: 5612587446 microseconds\n- Job ID: 6251995937\n- Task Index: 33\n- Event Type: 0 (SUBMIT)\n\n---\n\n## 2. JOB EVENTS TABLE SCHEMA\n\n**File Location:** `/app/workspace/data/job_events/part-00001-of-00500.csv.gz`\n\n**Total Columns:** 8\n\n### Column Definitions:\n\n| Column | Name | Data Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-----------|-------------|\n| 1 | **timestamp** | Integer (64-bit) | Event timestamp in **microseconds** since 600 seconds before trace start (May 1, 2011 19:00 EDT) |\n| 2 | missing_info | String | Empty string when no missing data; otherwise contains missing data indicators |\n| 3 | **job_id** | Integer | Unique identifier for the job |\n| 4 | **event_type** | Integer | Type of event (see event types below) |\n| 5 | user | String (Base64) | Hashed username for confidentiality |\n| 6 | scheduling_class | Integer | Latency sensitivity: 0=free, 1=best effort, 2-3=mid-tier, 4+=production |\n| 7 | job_name | String (Base64) | Hashed logical job name |\n| 8 | logical_job_name | String (Base64) | Hashed logical job name (alternative identifier) |\n\n### Event Type Values for Job Events:\n- **0 = SUBMIT** - Job is submitted to the system\n- **1 = SCHEDULE** - Job is scheduled\n- **3 = FAIL** - Job fails\n- **4 = KILL** - Job is killed\n- **5 = FINISH** - Job completes successfully\n\n**Note:** Event type 2 (EVICT) is not present in the job events data, as jobs are not evicted (only tasks are).\n\n**Sample Job Event (SUBMIT):**\n```\n5636908423,,6252021948,0,XzZHJR6eXZamIB7lSFTc/NXTbAKtt3SoOI8Fp/RtnwU=,2,Dak9tgVohhwVjNUJs8UZ4GON38RQ6n1KXgCOPK1NdSc=,oVQW4BB6g9OxJY1p0jZg3hr00UZ169KuGc0FzEDJoUE=\n```\n- Timestamp: 5636908423 microseconds\n- Job ID: 6252021948\n- Event Type: 0 (SUBMIT)\n\n---\n\n## KEY FINDINGS:\n\n1. **Timestamp Format:** Both tables use timestamps in **microseconds** (not seconds or milliseconds)\n2. **SUBMIT Event Value:** **0** represents a SUBMIT event in both tables\n3. **Job ID Location:** Column 3 in both tables\n4. **Task Index:** Only in Task Events table (Column 4)\n5. **Event Type Location:** Column 6 in Task Events, Column 4 in Job Events\n6. **Missing Info Field:** Column 2 is typically empty, indicating complete data\n\n---\n\n## Sources:\n- [Google Cluster Data GitHub Repository](https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/ClusterData2011_2.md)\n- [Google Cluster Usage Traces PDF Schema](https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Auday-Al-Dulaimy/post/Are-there-any-datasets-for-cloudSim/attachment/59d61de379197b807797be3e/AS:273823268573184@1442295962733/download/Google+cluster+usage+traces.pdf)\n- [Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.01426)\n- [Google Cluster Trace Dataset Overview](https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/google-cluster-trace-dataset)"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ad03678 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]}]},"uuid":"d4c91165-f1b0-4289-9889-d4c1714544af","timestamp":"2026-01-29T04:52:29.626Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Read the /app/workspace/data/format.pdf file and extract the schema information for:\n1. Task events - what are the column names and their meanings (especially timestamp, job ID, task index, event type)\n2. Job events - what are the column names and their meanings (especially timestamp, job ID, event type)\n\nFocus on understanding which columns contain the timestamp (in microseconds), job ID, task index, and event type fields. Also identify what event type value represents a SUBMIT event.","agentId":"ad03678","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Now I have all the information needed. Let me create a comprehensive summary document.\n\n## Schema Information Extraction Summary\n\nBased on my analysis of the Google Cluster Trace 2011-2 dataset at `/app/workspace/data/`, I've successfully extracted the schema information for both Task Events and Job Events tables.\n\n---\n\n## 1. TASK EVENTS TABLE SCHEMA\n\n**File Location:** `/app/workspace/data/task_events/part-00001-of-00500.csv.gz`\n\n**Total Columns:** 13\n\n### Column Definitions:\n\n| Column | Name | Data Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-----------|-------------|\n| 1 | **timestamp** | Integer (64-bit) | Event timestamp in **microseconds** since 600 seconds before trace start (May 1, 2011 19:00 EDT) |\n| 2 | missing_info | String | Empty string when no missing data; otherwise contains missing data indicators |\n| 3 | **job_id** | Integer | Unique identifier for the job |\n| 4 | **task_index** | Integer | 0-based index of the task within the job |\n| 5 | machine_id | Integer | ID of the machine where the task is/was running (empty for SUBMIT events) |\n| 6 | **event_type** | Integer | Type of event (see event types below) |\n| 7 | user | String (Base64) | Hashed username for confidentiality |\n| 8 | scheduling_class | Integer | Latency sensitivity: 0=free, 1=best effort, 2-3=mid-tier, 4+=production |\n| 9 | priority | Integer | Priority level (0-11, where higher = more important) |\n| 10 | cpu_request | Float | Requested CPU cores (normalized) |\n| 11 | memory_request | Float | Requested memory (normalized) |\n| 12 | disk_space_request | Float | Requested disk space (normalized) |\n| 13 | different_machines_restriction | Boolean | 0 or 1 indicating if tasks must run on different machines |\n\n### Event Type Values for Task Events:\n- **0 = SUBMIT** - Task is submitted to the system\n- **1 = SCHEDULE** - Task is scheduled on a machine\n- **2 = EVICT** - Task is evicted from a machine\n- **3 = FAIL** - Task fails\n- **4 = KILL** - Task is killed\n- **5 = FINISH** - Task completes successfully\n\n**Sample Task Event (SUBMIT):**\n```\n5612587446,,6251995937,33,,0,4Ubmtvv/epOnUEgegvGV9mCxxcZkV4z/Dm8RY/9SEYw=,0,0,0.06873,0.01193,0.0001154,0\n```\n- Timestamp: 5612587446 microseconds\n- Job ID: 6251995937\n- Task Index: 33\n- Event Type: 0 (SUBMIT)\n\n---\n\n## 2. JOB EVENTS TABLE SCHEMA\n\n**File Location:** `/app/workspace/data/job_events/part-00001-of-00500.csv.gz`\n\n**Total Columns:** 8\n\n### Column Definitions:\n\n| Column | Name | Data Type | Description |\n|--------|------|-----------|-------------|\n| 1 | **timestamp** | Integer (64-bit) | Event timestamp in **microseconds** since 600 seconds before trace start (May 1, 2011 19:00 EDT) |\n| 2 | missing_info | String | Empty string when no missing data; otherwise contains missing data indicators |\n| 3 | **job_id** | Integer | Unique identifier for the job |\n| 4 | **event_type** | Integer | Type of event (see event types below) |\n| 5 | user | String (Base64) | Hashed username for confidentiality |\n| 6 | scheduling_class | Integer | Latency sensitivity: 0=free, 1=best effort, 2-3=mid-tier, 4+=production |\n| 7 | job_name | String (Base64) | Hashed logical job name |\n| 8 | logical_job_name | String (Base64) | Hashed logical job name (alternative identifier) |\n\n### Event Type Values for Job Events:\n- **0 = SUBMIT** - Job is submitted to the system\n- **1 = SCHEDULE** - Job is scheduled\n- **3 = FAIL** - Job fails\n- **4 = KILL** - Job is killed\n- **5 = FINISH** - Job completes successfully\n\n**Note:** Event type 2 (EVICT) is not present in the job events data, as jobs are not evicted (only tasks are).\n\n**Sample Job Event (SUBMIT):**\n```\n5636908423,,6252021948,0,XzZHJR6eXZamIB7lSFTc/NXTbAKtt3SoOI8Fp/RtnwU=,2,Dak9tgVohhwVjNUJs8UZ4GON38RQ6n1KXgCOPK1NdSc=,oVQW4BB6g9OxJY1p0jZg3hr00UZ169KuGc0FzEDJoUE=\n```\n- Timestamp: 5636908423 microseconds\n- Job ID: 6252021948\n- Event Type: 0 (SUBMIT)\n\n---\n\n## KEY FINDINGS:\n\n1. **Timestamp Format:** Both tables use timestamps in **microseconds** (not seconds or milliseconds)\n2. **SUBMIT Event Value:** **0** represents a SUBMIT event in both tables\n3. **Job ID Location:** Column 3 in both tables\n4. **Task Index:** Only in Task Events table (Column 4)\n5. **Event Type Location:** Column 6 in Task Events, Column 4 in Job Events\n6. **Missing Info Field:** Column 2 is typically empty, indicating complete data\n\n---\n\n## Sources:\n- [Google Cluster Data GitHub Repository](https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/ClusterData2011_2.md)\n- [Google Cluster Usage Traces PDF Schema](https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Auday-Al-Dulaimy/post/Are-there-any-datasets-for-cloudSim/attachment/59d61de379197b807797be3e/AS:273823268573184@1442295962733/download/Google+cluster+usage+traces.pdf)\n- [Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.01426)\n- [Google Cluster Trace Dataset Overview](https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/google-cluster-trace-dataset)"}],"totalDurationMs":241363,"totalTokens":43464,"totalToolUseCount":37,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":430,"cache_read_input_tokens":43027,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":430,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c92a5d0c-a318-470b-966f-27d2be116b70"}
